ng because it *is* wrong. So I'll say this plainly: the FICA tax is not equitable in the way it treats wage earners versus investment earners. It is not equitable in the way the cap shields the highest earners. And if I were your dad, I'd probably feel the same way you do. What I would still defend is the *idea* of a contributory social insurance system—one where people who work can count on a secure retirement and healthcare. But the current structure needs reform. And stories like your dad's are exactly why. Thank you for sharing that. It's a powerful reminder that behind every policy debate, there are real people whose lives are shaped by these choices.
